Keep SimpleCPUOffload's CPU KV buffers unpinned under NVIDIA Confidential
Computing.

Upstream PR vllm-project/vllm#69432 (Privasys/vllm cpu-kv-offload-cc,
62556f767), runtime file only; the diff applies unchanged onto v0.34.0.

The connector pins its CPU KV buffers with cudaHostRegister, which the H100
refuses for guest memory in CC mode, so `--kv-offloading-size` killed the
engine at start (prod Imperial 2026-11-23 00:35, reverted). With this the
buffers stay in the TD's private anonymous mapping, unpinned, and the DMA
backend copies from pageable memory. Measured on Imperial with this exact
change on main: 6,336 of 6,505 prompt tokens reloaded from the CPU tier,
TTFT 0.196 s vs 4.47 s cold, output byte-identical to the GPU-cache hit.

diff --git a/vllm/v1/simple_kv_offload/worker.py b/vllm/v1/simple_kv_offload/worker.py
index cac204c14..7160569e6 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/simple_kv_offload/worker.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/simple_kv_offload/worker.py
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ import torch
 
 from vllm.config import VllmConfig
 from vllm.logger import init_logger
+from vllm.platforms import current_platform
 from vllm.utils.host_memory import (
     host_registration_ranges,
     pin_tensor,
@@ -245,7 +246,15 @@ class SimpleCPUOffloadWorker:
         )
 
         pin_memory = PIN_MEMORY
-        if not pin_memory:
+        if pin_memory and current_platform.is_confidential_compute():
+            # The GPU cannot register guest memory under Confidential
+            # Computing; copies from pageable memory still work.
+            logger.info(
+                "NVIDIA Confidential Computing detected; CPU offload buffers "
+                "are not pinned."
+            )
+            pin_memory = False
+        elif not pin_memory:
             logger.warning(
                 "Pinned memory not available. CPU offload performance may be degraded."
             )
